cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the paper; this repository supplies its LaTeX source and its finite checks."
type: software
title: "Perfect play in a binary-scoring nonlocal game requires infinite dimension"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-29
abstract: "We construct a finite rational two-player nonlocal game with ten Alice questions, eleven Bob questions, at most six answers per question and 52 equally likely supported pairs. It has a perfect spatial strategy and no perfect finite-dimensional strategy. For arbitrary finite-dimensional local POVMs and mixed states, its dimension profile is D_Gamma(epsilon) = 10 log2(1/epsilon) + O(log log(1/epsilon)). The lower bound is 10 log2(1/epsilon) - 10 log2 log2(1/epsilon) - O(1). A direct square-root magic-square extraction, robust flagged sector law and approximate gluing force twenty Schmidt coefficients per appreciable halving level. The explicit strategy compressed to 20K dimensions has loss exactly 1/[624(4^K-1)], yielding the matching leading upper coefficient 10."
